# Workflow Patterns

## Standard Patterns

### 1. Webhook → Process → Respond
Synchronous pattern for API-style workflows.
```
Webhook Trigger → Validate Input → Transform → Action → Respond to Webhook
```

### 2. Schedule → Fetch → Process → Notify
Batch processing pattern for periodic tasks.
```
Schedule Trigger → Fetch Data → Filter/Transform → Bulk Action → Notify Result
```

### 3. Event → Enrich → Route → Act
Event-driven pattern with conditional branching.
```
Event Trigger → Enrich Data → IF/Switch → [Branch A] / [Branch B] → Merge → Notify
```

### 4. AI Agent Loop
Autonomous agent pattern with tool use.
```
Trigger → AI Agent → [Tool calls] → Validate Output → Store Result → Notify
```

### 5. Error Handling Pattern
Standard error capture and notification.
```
Any node failure → Error Trigger → Format Error → Notify (Slack/Email) → Log to DB
```

## Anti-patterns

- **God workflows** — one workflow doing more than one thing
- **Hardcoded credentials** — always use n8n credential store
- **Silent failures** — every workflow must have an error handler
- **Undocumented branches** — every IF/Switch branch must have a sticky note
